{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.a3_near_miss_is_scale_ambiguous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.a3_near_miss_is_scale_ambiguous","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A3UnitsConsistency.lean#L59-L69","doc":"**Capstone — the A=3 near-miss is scale-ambiguous, not a units-correctable near-miss.** The gap is\na 3.53× undershoot under one normalization (`gap_A_undershoot_gt_three`) and a 1.66× overshoot under\nthe scale-consistent one (`gap_B_overshoot_between_one_two`); the two span the unpinned open gate\n`C_knot > 5` (`c_knot_gt_five`). So repairing the dimensional pun does not yield a single honest gap —\nthe real open object is `C_knot` itself (the Δ_λ magnitude). scope-(a) calibration + self-correction;\nno fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.normalizations_differ_by_c_knot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.normalizations_differ_by_c_knot","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A3UnitsConsistency.lean#L51-L57","doc":"**The two normalizations differ by exactly `C_knot`** (`(c₃/B_cat)/(c₃/B_AME) = B_AME/B_cat`), so\nthe A=3 gap swings across the whole open-gate factor — a 1.66× overshoot to a 3.53× undershoot. The\n\"1.6× near-miss\" is therefore an artifact of the unpinned categorical binding scale, not a robust\nproximity. (Instance of `units_correction_is_scale` with `c = c₃`, `B = B_AME/B_cat`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.gap_B_overshoot_between_one_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.gap_B_overshoot_between_one_two","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A3UnitsConsistency.lean#L43-L48","doc":"**Normalization B (÷ categorical deuteron, scale-consistent): a 1.66× OVERshoot.** With the\nmodel's own deuteron the scale `E₀/m_e` cancels, giving `(c₃/B_cat)/μ₃` strictly between 1 and 2 — an\novershoot, the opposite sign of normalization A. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.gap_A_undershoot_gt_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.gap_A_undershoot_gt_three","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A3UnitsConsistency.lean#L40-L41","doc":"**Normalization A (÷ AME deuteron): a 3.53× UNDERshoot.** `μ₃ / (c₃/B_AME) > 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.c_knot_gt_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.c_knot_gt_five","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A3UnitsConsistency.lean#L35-L38","doc":"**`C_knot` — the open Δ_λ gate.** The master formula `B = m_e·|Σ y_λ χ^λ sgn f^λ|` undershoots the\ndeuteron: `C_knot = B_AME(²H)/B_cat(²H) = 2.224566/0.380132 > 5` (≈5.85×), an explicitly FITTED (not\nderived) deficit ratio. This unpinned scale is what makes the A=3 gap ambiguous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.units_correction_is_scale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3UnitsConsistency.units_correction_is_scale","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A3UnitsConsistency.lean#L27-L33","doc":"**The correction factor is exactly `B`.** Comparing a MeV energy `c` to a dimensionless target `μ`\ngives the punned gap `μ/c`; the dimensionally-consistent gap divides the energy by the scale `B`\n(`c ↦ c/B`), giving `μ/(c/B)`. Their ratio is exactly `B`:\n`(μ/(c/B)) / (μ/c) = B`. Here `B = B(²H)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}